# tally 2.2.1 R21 (#221: 221.2, 221.4 and the plan's three cells), L §8.2 `unknown day:`: "the cell a caller pins,
# wherever a cell holds or copies the day …; where no cell does, its movement …; two days never share a line", and
# HOLE-IMPRECISE "one question per unknown day": a window written in a def is the def's (o2 `wr`), an observed row's
# field copied by a def the def's cell (hf `held_from[bank[g1]]`), one written in a move's own `on` its movement (o1
# `salary`), two moves with equal windows two lines (o3, pin), days_between of two windows two questions (two). tally
# 2.2 printed the window's text, one line for equal windows, and the first window's question only.
# tally 2.3 (G1, #247): a window that reaches a move's `on` or `at` makes it a hole day (L §4.4 A movement takes a
# day, §5.14): the movement's places are the hole on every day, HOLE-IMPRECISE naming the day; re-stored.
# tally 2.3 (G2, #247): re-stored: L §4.4's list reads a window by a closed list, and every other reader (days_between,
# end_of, weekday, a number) is the hole naming the day, so the hole is made at that reader.
=== r21.tally
model r21
  tally 2
  on 2026-08-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind gift: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  attr bought: date
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input d0: date
input d1: date
input w: date
input w0: date
input amt: money PLN
def wr: date = window(d0, d1)
def held_from[g in gift]: date = g.bought
move salary: transfers
  on window(d0, d1)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move bonus: transfers
  on wr
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
move twin: transfers
  on window(d0, d1)
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d0 = 2026-03-27 "s"
  d1 = 2026-03-31 "s"
  w = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  w0 = window(2026-03-12, 2026-03-14) "s"
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  bank[g1] = (on: 2026-04-10, kind: gift, leg cash from world to konto amount 50.00 PLN, bought: window(2019-01-01, 2019-12-31)) "g1"
ask o1: flows(salary, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-28)
ask o2: flows(bonus, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-28)
ask o3: bal(konto, 2026-03-29)
ask hf: held_from[bank[g1]] < 2019-06-01
ask two: days_between(w, w0)
ask pin: bal(konto, 2026-03-29) with wr = 2026-03-28
=== expect
hf: ?"date within window(2019-01-01, 2019-12-31) not precise enough for held_from[bank[g1]] < 2019-06-01" (held_from[bank[g1]])
  unknown day: held_from[bank[g1]]
  cut 2026-08-01
o1: ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of salary" (salary)
  unknown day: salary
  cut 2026-08-01
o2: ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of bonus" (wr)
  unknown day: wr
  cut 2026-08-01
o3: ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of bonus" (wr) ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of salary" (salary) ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of twin" (twin)
  unknown day: salary
  unknown day: twin
  unknown day: wr
  cut 2026-08-01
pin: ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of salary" (salary) ?"date within window(2026-03-27, 2026-03-31) not precise enough for the day of twin" (twin)
  pinned: wr = 2026-03-28
  unknown day: salary
  unknown day: twin
  unfulfilled: bonus
  cut 2026-08-01
two: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for days_between" (w) ?"date within window(2026-03-12, 2026-03-14) not precise enough for days_between" (w0)
  unknown day: w
  unknown day: w0
  cut 2026-08-01
